<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>Equations of Two Lines and a Curve</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02534</md:content-id>
    <md:title>Equations of Two Lines and a Curve</md:title>
    <md:uuid>7bce4292-5232-4194-ab88-feeae6a0144c</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>Write an equation representing the line that passes through each pair of points.</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>\((3,3)\) and \((5,5)\)</item>
  <item>\((0,4)\) and \((-4,0)\)</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>Solve this equation: \(x+1=(x−2)^2−3\). Show your reasoning.</item>
</list></section>
</content>
</document>
